275e|n|A bladderlike vessel; a membranous cavity; a cyst; a cell. ; A small bladderlike body in the substance of vegetable, or upon the surface of a leaf. ; A small, and more or less circular, elevation of the cuticle, containing a clear watery fluid. ; A cavity or sac, especially one filled with fluid; as, the umbilical vesicle. ; A small convex hollow prominence on the surface of a shell or a coral. ; A small cavity, nearly spherical in form, and usually of the size of a pea or smaller, such as are common in some volcanic rocks. They are produced by the liberation of watery vapor in the molten mass.	a:1ten,110,2;1uus,36,3~1uus,36,3;1ten,110,2	v:23bb,73,3~23bb,73,3	V:9i2,119,2;23bb,85,7;ttd,84,7;f70,58,3~ttd,84,7;23bb,85,7;f70,58,3;9i2,119,2	N:232o,139,3;9i2,109,1;sxj,88,6;18ui,76,3;1kb6,67,3;1p90,42,3;1v0x,30,3~sxj,88,6;232o,139,3;18ui,76,3;1v0x,30,3;1kb6,67,3;1p90,42,3;9i2,109,1
